# Persistent Storage

Persistent storage means saving important data so it does not disappear when the server restarts.

Right now our project uses `MemoryVectorStore`.

That is good for learning, but it lives only in memory.

If the backend restarts:

```text
Indexed chunks disappear.
Vector store disappears.
Chat history disappears.
The user must index the PDFs again.
```

Persistent storage fixes this.

## What We Should Store

A real RAG app should store:

```text
users
uploaded files
document records
chunks
embeddings
conversations
messages
token usage
indexing status
```

## Simple Example

When a user uploads:

```text
company-x-branch-morocco.pdf
```

We should save a document record:

```js
{
  id: "doc_001",
  fileName: "company-x-branch-morocco.pdf",
  status: "indexed",
  chunkCount: 135,
  uploadedAt: "2026-05-24"
}
```

Then we save chunks:

```js
{
  id: "chunk_001",
  documentId: "doc_001",
  page: 6,
  chunkIndex: 40,
  text: "CX-MA-001 - Amina Morrison..."
}
```

Then we save embeddings in a vector database or vector-enabled database.

## Why It Matters

Persistent storage allows:

```text
Server restart without losing data
Document history
Chat history
User accounts
Document deletion
Document re-indexing
Production deployment
```

## Simple Presentation Version

```text
Persistent storage saves documents, chunks, embeddings, and conversations permanently, so the app does not lose everything when the server restarts.
```

